498:In case $\cH$ is a collection of $K_s$-factors for $s >2$, the spread condition~\eqref{eq:def-spread} is slightly more difficult to verify, so it is convenient to pass to the setting of $s$-uniform hypergraphs, which is also done in~\cite{psss22}. In our applications, the ground set $Z$ will be an $s$-uniform hypergraph ($s$-graph), so given a graph $F$, let $F^{(s)}$ denote the collection of $K_s$-copies in $F$. For an $s$-graph $H$, let $\partial H$ denote the set of pairs contained in elements of $H$ (i.e.,~the 1-skeleton of $H$). We will be constructing spread measures on $F^{(s)}$ (for suitable $F$), which significantly simplifies the spread calculation~\eqref{eq:def-spread}, and then apply beautiful results due to Heckel~\cite{heckel21} and Riordan~\cite{riordan22} which immediately imply the desired threshold in random graphs.\footnote{Passing to hypergraphs also saves a $polylog$-factor in the threshold probability, but this is not needed for our application.}
