1211:Let $\delta >0$ and let $g$ be a positive integer. A \emph{$(\delta, g)$-absorber} $\absorber$ in an $n$-vertex graph $G$ is a collection of copies of $K_g$ in $G$ covering at most $\delta n$ vertices such that for every $x \in V(G)$, there are at least $\frac{\delta^2}{24g^2} n$ cliques in $\absorber$ containing a  neighbour of $x$. 
